        "problem": "Solve $2(x+7)^{2}+4\\le -6.$",
        "worked_solution": "Isolating the quadratic term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+7)^{2}+4 & \\le -6 \\\\ 2(x+7)^{2} & \\le -10 \\\\ (x+7)^{2} & \\le -5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $(x+7)^{2}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(2)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, there is no solution to the given inequality.",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
